OL,3,GNEWSAMother with disabled son fears
OL,4,Arise in intolerance
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of a boy with autism has
OL,7,Fsaid she is worried society is
OL,8,Fbeginning to feel less tolerant towards
OL,9,Fher son.
OL,11,FDarrell said her son Dexter, from
OL,12,FDevon, also had difficulties with
OL,13,Fspeech and the mindset of a much
OL,14,Fyounger child - but his disabilities
OL,15,Fwere not immediately obvious.
OL,17,FShe described him as "the most lovely
OL,18,Flad in the world" but said he had
OL,19,Fexperienced unpleasant encounters in
OL,20,Fpublic.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
